MULTIMODAL CHATBOT SOLUTIONS 
Consolidated Requirements & Specifications Document 
(Projects 1, 2 & 3) 
1. Purpose of This Document 
This document defines the full requirements and technical specifications for three chatbot 
solutions to be designed, tested, and demonstrated by trainees or project teams. 
The focus is on: 
● Clear problem understanding 
● Practical, implementable requirements 
● Multimodal AI chatbot design 
● Governance, compliance, and escalation 
● Fast implementation using flexible AI models 
2. Common Requirements (Applies to All Chatbot 
Projects) 
2.1 Multimodal Requirement 
All chatbot solutions must be multimodal by design, supporting: 
● Text-based interaction (mandatory) 
● Menu or button-based responses 
● Optional voice interaction 
● Optional document-aware interaction 
2.2 AI / LLM Model Requirement 
Each chatbot may use any of the following: 
● OpenAI models 
● Google models (e.g. Gemini) 
● Free or open-source LLMs 
The solution must: 
● Be model-agnostic 
● Allow switching models without redesigning logic 
● Prioritise accuracy and governance over creativity 
2.3 Trainee-Created Interfaces (Testing Only) 
For testing and demonstration: 
● Trainees may create their own interfaces 
● Interfaces may be web-based, CLI, or mock chat UIs 
● No production deployment is required 
● UI design quality is not assessed 
2.4 Architecture Overview 
Each chatbot must logically include: 
1. User Interaction Layer 
2. Conversation & Logic Layer 
3. AI / LLM Layer 
4. Knowledge & Content Layer 
5. Escalation & Handover Layer 
6. Logging & Reporting Layer 
PROJECT 1: mLab Website Visitor 
Chatbot 
1. Overview & Problem Description 
mLab receives a high volume of website enquiries related to programmes, applications, 
eligibility, locations, and events. These enquiries are handled manually, leading to delayed 
responses, inconsistent information, and administrative strain. 
The chatbot aims to provide instant, consistent, and accurate visitor support, while 
reducing manual workload and improving engagement. 
2. Scope 
In Scope 
● Visitor enquiries via website 
● Programme and application information 
● Location and event details 
● Enquiry logging 
● Escalation to administrative staff 
Out of Scope 
● Internal staff systems 
● Payments or financial transactions 
● Marketing campaign management 
● Personal academic advice 
3. Functional Requirements 
● Greet visitors and explain chatbot purpose 
● Provide menu-based enquiry categories 
● Answer programme and application-related questions 
● Support free-text questions 
● Escalate unresolved queries 
● Log all enquiries and outcomes 
4. Non-Functional Requirements 
● 24/7 availability 
● Response time ≤ 3 seconds for standard queries 
● POPIA-compliant data handling 
● Simple, user-friendly language 
5. Business Rules 
● Only approved content may be used 
● No personalised advice 
● No collection of mandatory personal data 
6. Acceptance Criteria 
● Visitors can obtain accurate information without human support 
● Escalation works correctly 
● Enquiries are logged and reportable 